  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nAnomalous mid level ridge extending from the lower Mississippi\nValley into the Great Lakes will gradually lose amplitude during the \nearly part of the week as several pieces of energy lift out of the \nwestern US into the Great Lakes. Flow will briefly become zonal mid \nweek with low amplitude ridging returning late in the week. At the \nsurface, a weak front will sag south into the area Monday into Monday\nnight and then wash out by Tuesday night into Wednesday. Otherwise, \nhigh pressure will predominate. Low to mid levels will remain dry \nthrough the week, so the extended dry period will persist.\n\nTemperatures will remain above normal, but daily diurnal ranges will\nnarrow a bit as lows warm up into the upper 40s to lower 50s by mid\nweek.",
